{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization proving Written on the Wall II Conjecture 61: for every nontrivial finite connected simple graph G, the maximum order f(G) of an induced forest satisfies f(G) ≥ residue(G) + ⌈diam(G) / 3⌉, where residue(G) is the Havel-Hakimi residue and diam(G) is the graph diameter. The proof establishes positive maximum-degree vertex-deletion monotonicity for Havel-Hakimi residue from first principles via degree-sequence exchanges and Havel-Hakimi graphicality, proves a matching-residue theorem yielding the general Induced-Matching Residue Inequality R(G) ≤ max(α(G - A), α(G - B)) for every induced matching A ↔ B in any finite simple graph G, applies it to ⌈diam(G) / 3⌉ edges along a diametral geodesic whose sides are 3-packings, and lifts the bound to the exact real-valued statement in google-deepmind/formal-conjectures using only the three standard Lean axioms.",
  "authors": [
